<section class="panel" aria-label="2021 Grade 3 Information Gap source method with first-party cards"><h2>Warm-up: Number Talk — Two Steps</h2><p>Original source 20+2×3=26;30+4×3=42;50+8×3=74;99+8×3=123. Explain how equal groups and additional quantities fit.</p><h2>Activity 1: Information Gap — Chairs</h2><p><strong>Problem Card (independent Edulytics example)</strong>: How many chairs are in a room? Ask another student for how many rows, chairs in each row and loose chairs in the corner. Do not reveal the values before they explain why needed.</p><details><summary>Data Card (partner only)</summary><p>3 rows, 6 chairs per row and4 more chairs. Solution 3×6+4=22.</p></details><h2>Activity 2: Information Gap — Bake Sale</h2><p><strong>Problem Card (independent Edulytics example)</strong>: How many muffins were prepared? Ask for trays, muffins per tray and additional muffins.</p><details><summary>Data Card (partner only)</summary><p>5 trays, 8 muffins per tray and13 extra muffins. Solution 5×8+13=53.</p></details><p>Teacher may use source ORIGINAL publisher Bake Sale cards separately; their numbers were not accessible in local source text and we do not claim parity. Students switch roles and compare reasoning.</p><a href="https://im.kendallhunt.com/k5/teachers/grade-3/unit-3/lesson-20/lesson.html">Original 2021 teacher reference</a></section>